lds vs learned detectors.","checklist":["List failure modes of slope thresholds"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["6f1299b1-42f6-5b8d-9b87-5b49fd54383c"]},{"id":"dabd4000-2a7d-5a53-9072-19760c94dc1e","path_id":"9a4e8514-3cdb-54dd-a763-4fd6b70a4a1e","order":7,"title":"Traversability mapping","objective":"Combine layers into costs.","checklist":["Map slope/roughness to OccupancyGrid values"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["a90c1792-89cb-532d-a2b3-d146f8d8141b","ca85ca36-be1a-5017-a601-05df5375fb6e"]},{"id":"cf21a111-300f-5d41-b668-aa8fec2764f8","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":0,"title":"URDF","objective":"Links, joints, inertia.","checklist":["Write a two-link URDF","check_urdf"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["87f943be-21c8-56cc-bd51-e29e089e9a00","cb882370-9061-5048-b032-66e0376ed2d4"]},{"id":"39883084-d25c-5db9-a57c-900a65d80196","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":1,"title":"Xacro","objective":"Properties and macros.","checklist":["Refactor with a wheel macro"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["bc7d5e94-c943-56cb-b79c-f9763553e78c"]},{"id":"3d8e9c08-1b0f-50b8-900e-156729893c13","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":2,"title":"ROS TF","objective":"robot_state_publisher output.","checklist":["Visualize TF in RViz"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["48d88130-ebb2-50e8-a73f-0c1df1ba777b"]},{"id":"9bfa07d4-ffb0-537f-a887-4636bf9f4198","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":3,"title":"Gazebo","objective":"Worlds and models.","checklist":["Run getting started","Write a world file"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["d551ccf3-3b44-5f71-a5cb-996ecf360935","20615bd3-848f-55fb-ab76-08846fe13557","b523b33e-c38e-59e3-beba-0139a9cc335e"]},{"id":"6d652499-ab88-5ecd-8dfc-c406173714f7","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":4,"title":"Physics","objective":"Friction and contacts.","checklist":["Change friction and observe slip"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["5e5a60bd-ca1a-50f9-913d-ae9170c78345","f9469dca-4ff0-5bb1-84a0-9538a45aef3a"]},{"id":"134c6ed0-c945-52ed-b444-1fb07f25c160","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":5,"title":"Sensors","objective":"Simulated LiDAR/IMU/camera.","checklist":["Add an IMU and LiDAR to a model","Bridge to ROS 2"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["4cbed166-f914-5a76-a384-58aaf16d4896","5bc659ce-ac67-5c98-8285-9a73a5d91cce"]},{"id":"934122bc-eb21-549d-98b7-82ba08655d95","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":6,"title":"Simulated drivetrain","objective":"Stand in for Controls in simulation only.","checklist":["Run a diff-drive demo","Drive it from the AG-07 mock topic"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["a7c43cc7-2baf-5cbb-81d6-c9e4467d3d7c","ef67bca1-0645-553c-99f3-83f6d495378e","7d1480cc-340b-57f6-804e-0ce157a74871"]},{"id":"9ce95b49-c106-5418-bab8-528bc38fad72","path_id":"9a1e4e90-bc4c-559c-a79f-97037bcbb385","order":7,"title":"Scenario design","objective":"Seeded, reproducible scenarios.","checklist":["Write a scenario YAML","Spawn it twice and compare"],"exercise":"Create a rock-field scenario for SIM-01.","resource_ids":["20615bd3-848f-55fb-ab76-08846fe13557"]},{"id":"6eec9691-4db1-5ff7-8f7f-9756269136f9","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":0,"title":"Topics, services and actions","objective":"Choose the right communication pattern.","checklist":["Explain when to use an action vs a topic","Write a minimal action client"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["54c635df-9476-5698-8046-9492aeb99971","d52f49f7-6681-5630-ab76-69ee37ada9ca"]},{"id":"1356dfc0-5f13-5bef-bc20-8747d618931e","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":1,"title":"Interfaces and conventions","objective":"Design shared messages and naming.","checklist":["Create a custom msg and action","Read REP-103/105"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["dd415d40-ef95-5397-8526-90d11b3f1e0a","a9d3d523-0225-5ccc-865c-0984777af6c1","724c3d71-073d-51fc-bce2-0f05570e1df6"]},{"id":"c9627897-51a6-56e3-a4d7-28d804ad60b0","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":2,"title":"Launch orchestration and QoS","objective":"Compose a stack reproducibly.","checklist":["Write a launch file with arguments","Pick QoS for status vs commands"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["f25dec27-c4cf-5762-a7b9-9643f1443b1f","30983abb-fbb0-5e0a-a475-5c9d5b7820c4"]},{"id":"d169b171-ffd2-521d-bf57-49c874afa69b","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":3,"title":"State machines vs behavior trees","objective":"Pick a mission structure.","checklist":["Watch both behavior-tree talks","Sketch our mission as an FSM"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["f3a54f40-9976-5a0c-932d-fe743f493b4b","4f7a858c-e5fe-5281-9da7-077ae4d5228f","884a4786-fd54-5ef7-8b11-9e8784da5ec1"]},{"id":"3ce18bab-6fc6-5fd6-9c3c-0f4085f39315","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":4,"title":"Team boundaries","objective":"Separate decisions from hardware control.","checklist":["Watch the ros2_control boundary video","List what autonomy requests vs what Controls executes"],"exercise":"Draft the fields of a ControlsStatus message for AG-07.","resource_ids":["54343c49-dce4-5edc-9575-351ff3794278","5cbab412-d11d-5c62-9a84-6221ca149c71"]},{"id":"0c5855aa-89e0-548f-8e64-74d0027b44d2","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":5,"title":"Recording and replay","objective":"Make tests reproducible.","checklist":["Record and replay a bag with --clock","Compute one metric from a bag"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["73298a07-2ed6-5224-99d5-c009df68ca5e","6f784f87-cfa7-5ead-a50c-c10257e214bd"]},{"id":"36a71ed8-fbc0-532c-ae00-a330bb5a08bc","path_id":"c28b3f7d-ca25-5081-910f-9935423f6675","order":6,"title":"End-to-end evaluation","objective":"Judge a whole mission run.","checklist":["Read the valid-demonstration ADR","Write pass criteria before running"],"exercise":null,"resource_ids":["788a889e-c6bf-5d2f-af0e-d66aee74b4be"]}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
insert into documents select * from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::documents, '[{"id":"4247911a-5136-5c9f-a95a-e66e219eb16a","slug":"autonomy-team-structure","title":"Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels","category":"onboarding","tags":["start-here","discord","scope"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels\n\nWe are the **Illinois Tech NASA Lunabotics 2027 Autonomy Team** — not the whole robotics organization. Every task belongs to exactly one of these five categories, each mapped to a Discord channel:\n\n| Discord channel | Category | Task prefix | Role |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🧠 autonomy-general | Autonomy General | AG | Coordination: ROS 2 architecture, mission logic, systems integration, testing & validation, interfaces to other teams |\n| 🕸️ sensor-fusion | Sensor Fusion & Localization | SF | Pose, velocity, orientation and confidence |\n| 📸 perception | Perception & Mapping | PM | Obstacles, terrain, maps and costmaps |\n| 🗺️ navigation | Navigation & Planning | NV | Goals, paths, Nav2, recovery |\n| 🕹️ simulations | Simulation & Digital Twin | SIM | Arena, rover model, sensors, scenarios, automation |\n\nAutonomy General is a coordination category, not a fifth technical subteam.\n\n## What autonomy owns\n\nSensing and estimation, mapping, obstacle detection, path planning, autonomous navigation, mission decisions, **high-level** excavation and deposition requests, simulation environments, ROS 2 integration and end-to-end testing in simulation.\n\n## What we do not build\n\n| Function | Owner |\n|---|---|\n| Motor PID, actuator control loops | Controls |\n| Motor drivers and firmware, CAN | Controls / Electrical |\n| Wiring and power distribution | Electrical |\n| Physical emergency-stop hardware | Controls / Electrical |\n| Excavation motor implementation | Controls |\n| Digging mechanism, drivetrain design | Mechanical |\n\nWe specify **interfaces** to these teams (see [External Team Interfaces](/docs/external-team-interfaces)) and use mocks until their parts exist. Former Control & Safety tasks (CS-01…CS-06, IT-05) are archived for history; their autonomy-side pieces moved to AG-07 and SF-06.\n\n## Old task IDs\n\nTasks keep their history when re-keyed, and old links redirect: MS-01→AG-01, MS-02→AG-02, MS-03→AG-03, IT-01→AG-04, IT-02→AG-05, IT-03→AG-06, IT-06→AG-08, MS-04→AG-09, MS-05→AG-10, MS-06→AG-11, CS-04→AG-12, IT-04→AG-13, SF-06→SF-08, SF-07→PM-09, PM-07↔PM-08 (swapped), NV-06→NV-08, NV-07→NV-06, SIM-04→SIM-06, SIM-05→SIM-04, SIM-06→SIM-05. Where an old key now names a different task (e.g. SF-06), the task page says so.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"637321fe-e426-5b02-b948-cafe14395c3f","slug":"external-team-interfaces","title":"External Team Interfaces","category":"architecture","tags":["interfaces","controls","electrical","mechanical"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# External Team Interfaces\n\nAutonomy depends on other teams for interfaces and data, never for us to build their systems. Each dependency is tracked on the 🧠 Autonomy General page with a status, a contact and our workaround.\n\n| Team | Provides to autonomy | Autonomy task | Workaround until delivered |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Controls | Motion command interface, enforced limits, status and faults (AG-07 contract) | AG-07, NV-02, AG-01 | Mock Controls node in simulation |\n| Controls | Excavation / deposition action servers | AG-02, AG-03 | Mock action servers |\n| Controls | Wheel odometry on hardware | SF-01 | Simulated drivetrain plugin |\n| Electrical | Sensor power and communication requirements; radar detection format | SF-05, SIM-04, PM-09 | Labeled assumptions |\n| Mechanical | Rover dimensions, mass properties, joints, mechanism constraints | SIM-02, PM-01, AG-03 | Clearly labeled approximations |\n| Hardware teams | Sensor specifications and mounting positions | SF-02, SIM-04 | Nominal CAD values, re-calibrated later |\n\n## Rules\n\n1. Autonomy never publishes motor-level commands (duty cycles, currents, actuator positions).\n2. Every motion request is timestamped; Controls rejects stale ones.\n3. Safe stop is a *request*; Controls executes it and re-enables motion.\n4. Interface documents live in `docs/interfaces/` and are versioned and reviewed by both teams.\n5. Autonomy completion metrics never count external work; external blockers are shown separately.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"6d2f1340-8af4-5216-88ad-557387252639","slug":"team-onboarding","title":"Team Onboarding","category":"onboarding","tags":["start-here"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Team Onboarding\n\nWelcome to the Illinois Tech Lunabotics **Autonomy Team**. Start with [Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels](/docs/autonomy-team-structure).\n\n## Your first week\n1. Sign in to the Command Center and fill in your profile (skills, availability, GitHub username).\n2. Start the **Beginner to ROS 2 Contributor** learning path. You can claim a beginner task after module 5 — you don''t need to finish every path first.\n3. Read [Development Environment Setup](/docs/development-environment-setup) and [Git Workflow](/docs/git-workflow).\n4. Browse **Task Board → Available** and express interest in tasks that fit your track.\n\n## How work flows here\n- Every task is a guided assignment: read the *Why this matters*, study the referenced code, then work through the checklist.\n- Log progress after each work session — it helps reviewers and the next person.\n- A task is done only when a reviewer approves it against its Definition of Done. Merged PRs alone do not complete tasks.\n\n## Where to ask\nUse task discussions for technical questions so answers stay with the work.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"02323238-403e-57d3-a170-cfe7053fcecc","slug":"development-environment-setup","title":"Development Environment Setup","category":"onboarding","tags":["setup","ros2"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Development Environment Setup\n\n> **Status:** draft. The ROS 2 distribution and Gazebo version are an open decision (see ADR \"Why ROS 2?\"). Update this page once decided.\n\n## Baseline (proposed)\n- Ubuntu LTS matching the chosen ROS 2 distribution\n- ROS 2 (Humble or Jazzy — decision pending)\n- Gazebo version paired with the ROS 2 distribution\n- colcon, rosdep, vcstool\n\n## Verify your install\n```bash\nros2 doctor\nros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker\n```\n\n## Workspace\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/lunabot_ws/src && cd ~/lunabot_ws\ncolcon build --symlink-install\nsource install/setup.bash\n```\n\nWindows/macOS members: document your working setup (VM, WSL2, container) here once verified.","status":"needs_review","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"3e4e0897-1c37-52dc-bfff-3e0a927683b3","slug":"git-workflow","title":"Git Workflow","category":"standards","tags":["git","github"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Git Workflow\n\n- Branch from `main`: `feature/<TASK-ID>-<short-slug>` — e.g. `feature/SF-01-sensor-fusion`.\n- Small, focused commits with imperative messages.\n- Open a PR titled `[TASK-ID] Summary` — e.g. `[SF-01] Implement initial localization estimator`.\n- Link the PR on the task page (GitHub section) so reviewers find it.\n- Rebase or merge `main` before requesting review; CI must pass.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"340adb23-bc3a-5654-b4eb-77236869d707","slug":"pull-request-standards","title":"Pull Request Standards","category":"standards","tags":["review","github"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Pull Request Standards\n\nEvery PR description includes:\n1. **Task** — link to the Command Center task.\n2. **What changed** — packages, nodes, parameters.\n3. **How to test** — exact commands.\n4. **Evidence** — plots, recordings, test output.\n5. **Interfaces** — any topic/message/frame changes (update the topic table).\n\nReviewers check functional correctness, documentation, tests, interface compatibility, performance, safety and integration readiness — the same dimensions used in task reviews.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2963146f-a287-5057-b1dc-6fd1ca9eba6c","slug":"ros2-package-conventions","title":"ROS 2 Package Conventions","category":"standards","tags":["ros2","conventions"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# ROS 2 Package Conventions (proposed — finalized by IT-01)\n\n- Package names: `lunabot_<area>` (snake_case).\n- Interfaces only in `lunabot_interfaces`.\n- Every tunable is a parameter; defaults live in `config/*.yaml`.\n- Pure logic in modules without ROS imports so it can be unit-tested.\n- Launch files in Python; accept `use_sim_time`.\n- Topics under subsystem namespaces: `/localization/*`, `/perception/*`, `/navigation/*`, `/mission/*`, `/autonomy/*` (requests to Controls). Controls-owned topics live under `/controls/*`.\n- QoS: SensorDataQoS for high-rate sensors; reliable + transient-local for state and health topics.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8802221a-846e-5ed8-bf0a-41e5d42e6c58","slug":"coordinate-frame-conventions","title":"Coordinate Frame Conventions","category":"standards","tags":["tf","frames"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Coordinate Frame Conventions\n\nFollow REP-103 (units, axes) and REP-105 (mobile platform frames).\n\n```\nmap ──► odom ──► base_link ──► lidar_link\n                         ├──► imu_link\n                         ├──► camera_link ──► camera_optical_frame\n                         └──► (radar_link)\n```\n\n| Transform | Owner (proposed) |\n|---|---|\n| map → odom | Absolute localization (AprilTag/SLAM) or static identity in early sim |\n| odom → base_link | SF-01 EKF (drivetrain controller must NOT publish it) |\n| base_link → sensors | URDF (SIM-02) using calibration values (SF-02) |","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"838a6a82-6d00-5e4e-8166-455d8d5f943a","slug":"sensor-interfaces","title":"Sensor Interfaces","category":"architecture","tags":["sensors","topics"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Sensor Interfaces (illustrative)\n\n| Topic | Type | Frame | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| /lidar/points | sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2 | lidar_link | Per-point time needed for LIO de-skew |\n| /imu/data | sensor_msgs/msg/Imu | imu_link | Covariances must be filled |\n| /wheel/odometry | nav_msgs/msg/Odometry | odom → base_link | From Controls feedback on hardware (AG-07); from the drivetrain plugin in simulation |\n| /camera/image_raw | sensor_msgs/msg/Image | camera_optical_frame | |\n\nThese become verified once IT-01''s topic table is approved and matching code is merged.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"3ddbfde6-2e32-5cde-9a41-3f90df3905e8","slug":"localization-architecture","title":"Localization Architecture","category":"architecture","tags":["localization"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Localization Architecture\n\nWheel odometry + IMU (+ LIO, SF-03) → EKF/UKF (SF-01) → /odometry/filtered and odom → base_link.\nSF-04 monitors health and publishes OK/DEGRADED/LOST to mission logic and the arbiter.\n\nOpen question: absolute map anchoring (AprilTags vs SLAM vs known start pose) — see ADR \"Which localization algorithm?\".","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2de121c5-abf6-5749-bbfd-4a7494201a38","slug":"perception-architecture","title":"Perception Architecture","category":"architecture","tags":["perception"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Perception Architecture\n\nLiDAR → PM-02 preprocessing (filter, crop, voxel, accumulate) → PM-01 terrain grid (elevation, slope, roughness) → traversability OccupancyGrid → Nav2 costmaps.\nCameras → AprilTags (PM-03), optionally rock detection (PM-05).","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"405b4dea-750f-560e-8b59-5eb2ed672693","slug":"navigation-architecture","title":"Navigation Architecture","category":"architecture","tags":["navigation","nav2"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Navigation Architecture\n\nNav2 bt_navigator executes a behavior tree that plans (NV-01 planner) on the traversability costmap and follows with a local controller. Velocity output goes through the AG-07 adapter to /autonomy/cmd_vel; Controls (mock Controls in simulation) executes it. Recovery follows NV-06''s BT.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"cdcf3098-01b0-5da3-8804-c6cc5e38f44d","slug":"simulation-setup","title":"Simulation Setup","category":"operations","tags":["gazebo","simulation"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Simulation Setup\n\n```bash\nros2 launch lunabot_sim arena.launch.py scenario:=rocks seed:=42\n```\n(Illustrative — the package is delivered by SIM-01.)\n\nScenarios are seeded YAML files so results are reproducible. Use the lite world on laptops and in CI.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"72ba1078-d327-5cae-83e4-685f9f98cb86","slug":"control-safety-architecture","title":"Autonomy ↔ Controls Boundary","category":"architecture","tags":["safety","controls","interfaces"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Autonomy ↔ Controls Boundary\n\nAutonomy publishes **timestamped motion requests** on /autonomy/cmd_vel through the AG-07 adapter, sends **safe-stop requests**, and reads **ControlsStatus** (mode, motion enabled, E-stop active, enforced limits, faults).\n\nControls owns teleoperation, command arbitration, watchdogs, motor control, firmware and the physical emergency stop. Former tasks CS-01…CS-06 are archived for that reason.\n\n**Software stops never replace the hardware E-stop.** The hardware E-stop cuts actuator power independently of any computer and is Controls/Electrical-owned.\n\nSee [External Team Interfaces](/docs/external-team-interfaces) and AG-07.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"6b18f653-a9bc-5255-b2ce-cda40f604ab9","slug":"testing-standards","title":"Testing Standards","category":"standards","tags":["testing"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Testing Standards\n\n- Pure logic has unit tests (`colcon test`).\n- Nodes have at least one launch/integration test or a documented replay test.\n- Benchmarks state machine, commit, scenario, seed and command.\n- Never report metrics without provenance; synthetic demo values must be labeled as such.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8c7d99db-fc69-54ac-8ee5-ad7720562be4","slug":"competition-requirements","title":"Competition Requirements and Verification","category":"competition","tags":["rules"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Competition Requirements and Verification\n\n**Rule of this page:** only requirements quoted from the *current* official NASA Lunabotics guidebook belong here, each with a section reference and the date it was checked. Other teams'' code is not a source of rules.\n\n| Requirement | Guidebook section | Verified on | Affects tasks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| _To be filled from the official guidebook_ | | | |\n\nInternal engineering targets (e.g. localization error goals) are **not** competition requirements and are tracked on tasks with rationale.","status":"needs_review","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"7757cfcd-0870-5a3a-b3d6-400209dfcd4d","slug":"troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","category":"operations","tags":["debugging"],"owner_id":null,"body":"# Troubleshooting\n\n**No data on a topic** — check `ros2 topic info -v` for QoS mismatch.\n\n**TF flickering** — two publishers of the same transform (often odom → base_link). `ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames`.\n\n**Nodes ignore bag data** — missing `--clock` or `use_sim_time:=true`.\n\n**Robot explodes in Gazebo** — zero/tiny inertias in the URDF.","status":"published","adr":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"042378b8-20dd-5e7f-b806-606479eb7823","slug":"adr-why-ros2","title":"ADR: Why ROS 2?","category":"decision","tags":["adr"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for the middleware choice.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"proposed","context":"We need a robotics framework with mature navigation, localization, simulation integration and community support. All four reference teams use ROS 2.","alternatives":[{"name":"ROS 2","pros":"Nav2, robot_localization, ros2_control, Gazebo bridge; reference teams'' code is reusable; large community.","cons":"Learning curve; DDS configuration issues."},{"name":"Custom framework (e.g. Rust/iceoryx as Utah partially uses)","pros":"Performance and control.","cons":"Rebuild navigation/localization from scratch; harder onboarding."}],"evidence":"Reference repositories (Purdue, COD, GOFIRST) are ROS 2 stacks; Utah uses ROS-adjacent components and its own tooling.","decision":"Proposed: ROS 2. Distribution (Humble vs Jazzy) still open — pick based on Gazebo pairing and hardware OS support.","tradeoffs":"Faster start and reuse versus some runtime overhead and DDS tuning."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"a468bd34-2552-52c8-aa09-9d0f078792b2","slug":"adr-gazebo-baseline","title":"ADR: Why Gazebo as the baseline simulator?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","simulation"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for the baseline simulator.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"proposed","context":"Every member must be able to run simulation; perception testing benefits from realistic rendering.","alternatives":[{"name":"Gazebo","pros":"Runs on ordinary laptops; native ROS 2 bridge; ros2_control integration.","cons":"Limited rendering realism and soil physics."},{"name":"Isaac Sim","pros":"Photoreal sensors; GPU acceleration.","cons":"Requires RTX GPU; heavier setup."},{"name":"MuJoCo","pros":"Fast, accurate contacts.","cons":"No native ROS 2 integration; fewer sensor models."}],"evidence":"COD and GOFIRST provide Gazebo worlds; GOFIRST also targets Isaac Sim; Utah uses MuJoCo.","decision":"Proposed: Gazebo as baseline; evaluate Isaac Sim (SIM-04) and MuJoCo (SIM-03) for specific needs.","tradeoffs":"Accessibility over realism for the baseline."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"e584b2e0-2210-5233-a918-85c607f91c5c","slug":"adr-localization","title":"ADR: Which localization algorithm?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","localization"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for localization.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"open","context":"Wheel slip on regolith makes wheel odometry unreliable.","alternatives":[{"name":"EKF (wheel + IMU)","pros":"Simple; robot_localization.","cons":"Drifts under slip."},{"name":"LIO (Point-LIO/FAST-LIO) fused in UKF","pros":"Robust to slip (COD approach).","cons":"Compute and sensor requirements."},{"name":"SLAM (RTAB-Map/slam_toolbox)","pros":"Global consistency.","cons":"Complexity; featureless terrain."}],"evidence":"Pending SF-01 and SF-03 benchmarks.","decision":"Open — decide from SF-01/SF-03 benchmark results.","tradeoffs":"Accuracy vs compute and integration effort."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"f48890b4-5064-58c8-badb-0607b3dafab7","slug":"adr-planner","title":"ADR: Which navigation planner?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","navigation"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for the global planner.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"open","context":"Turns cost time and cause slip; paths must respect terrain.","alternatives":[{"name":"A* / NavFn","pros":"Simple, robust.","cons":"Jagged paths."},{"name":"S-Theta* (Purdue)","pros":"Any-angle, turn-aware.","cons":"Custom code to maintain."},{"name":"Nav2 Theta* / Smac","pros":"Upstream maintained.","cons":"Tuning for our terrain."}],"evidence":"Pending NV-01 benchmark.","decision":"Open — decide from NV-01 results.","tradeoffs":"Path quality vs maintenance."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"b442a878-e2b6-5ce9-add0-ec778097295a","slug":"adr-sensors","title":"ADR: Which sensors?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","hardware"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for the sensor suite.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"open","context":"Sensor choice drives localization and perception design; must be coordinated with hardware, budget and rules.","alternatives":[{"name":"3D LiDAR + IMU + wheel encoders","pros":"Geometry-based perception and LIO.","cons":"Cost; dust sensitivity."},{"name":"Stereo/RGB-D cameras + IMU","pros":"Cheaper; texture info.","cons":"Lighting sensitivity."},{"name":"Add radar","pros":"Dust robustness.","cons":"Sparse; pending SF-05."}],"evidence":"Pending SF-05 and SIM-04; specifications come from Hardware/Electrical (external dependency).","decision":"Open.","tradeoffs":"Robustness vs cost/mass/power."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"14f40b7f-363a-5710-a05c-34469b60a122","slug":"adr-fallback-policy","title":"ADR: What is the autonomy fallback policy?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","safety"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for fallback behavior.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"proposed","context":"Faults will happen: localization loss, stalls, link loss.","alternatives":[{"name":"Stop and wait for operator","pros":"Simple, safe.","cons":"Loses autonomy time."},{"name":"Bounded autonomous recovery then stop","pros":"Keeps mission going.","cons":"More complexity (AG-10)."}],"evidence":"SF-04, NV-06, AG-07 designs.","decision":"Proposed: LOST localization, a Controls fault or an E-stop reported by Controls → SAFE_STOP (a safe-stop request through AG-07; Controls executes); recoverable faults → bounded recovery (NV-06 navigation, AG-10 mission) then SAFE_STOP.","tradeoffs":"Safety first; autonomy time second."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"14d3e1f0-4916-5dbf-8b77-38370f26ed0d","slug":"adr-valid-demo","title":"ADR: What constitutes a valid mission demonstration?","category":"decision","tags":["adr","readiness"],"owner_id":null,"body":"Decision record for the end-to-end demonstration criteria.","status":"draft","adr":{"status":"proposed","context":"Leadership needs an unambiguous signal that the autonomy stack works end-to-end.","alternatives":[{"name":"Any successful run","pros":"Easy.","cons":"Cherry-picking."},{"name":"AG-08 end-to-end run with recorded evidence","pros":"Reproducible.","cons":"Requires infrastructure."}],"evidence":"AG-05 and AG-08 designs.","decision":"Proposed: an AG-08 run from clean bringup in simulation, using estimated localization (no ground truth in the loop) and mock Controls/excavation/deposition, completing ≥ 1 full excavate→deposit cycle without human input, with a recording/bag linked as evidence. The readiness indicator is set only with that evidence.","tradeoffs":"Strictness over convenience."},"created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
insert into document_revisions select * from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::document_revisions, '[{"id":"3294b49e-8cde-5fb7-8890-daaa550eeb65","document_id":"4247911a-5136-5c9f-a95a-e66e219eb16a","body":"# Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels\n\nWe are the **Illinois Tech NASA Lunabotics 2027 Autonomy Team** — not the whole robotics organization. Every task belongs to exactly one of these five categories, each mapped to a Discord channel:\n\n| Discord channel | Category | Task prefix | Role |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🧠 autonomy-general | Autonomy General | AG | Coordination: ROS 2 architecture, mission logic, systems integration, testing & validation, interfaces to other teams |\n| 🕸️ sensor-fusion | Sensor Fusion & Localization | SF | Pose, velocity, orientation and confidence |\n| 📸 perception | Perception & Mapping | PM | Obstacles, terrain, maps and costmaps |\n| 🗺️ navigation | Navigation & Planning | NV | Goals, paths, Nav2, recovery |\n| 🕹️ simulations | Simulation & Digital Twin | SIM | Arena, rover model, sensors, scenarios, automation |\n\nAutonomy General is a coordination category, not a fifth technical subteam.\n\n## What autonomy owns\n\nSensing and estimation, mapping, obstacle detection, path planning, autonomous navigation, mission decisions, **high-level** excavation and deposition requests, simulation environments, ROS 2 integration and end-to-end testing in simulation.\n\n## What we do not build\n\n| Function | Owner |\n|---|---|\n| Motor PID, actuator control loops | Controls |\n| Motor drivers and firmware, CAN | Controls / Electrical |\n| Wiring and power distribution | Electrical |\n| Physical emergency-stop hardware | Controls / Electrical |\n| Excavation motor implementation | Controls |\n| Digging mechanism, drivetrain design | Mechanical |\n\nWe specify **interfaces** to these teams (see [External Team Interfaces](/docs/external-team-interfaces)) and use mocks until their parts exist. Former Control & Safety tasks (CS-01…CS-06, IT-05) are archived for history; their autonomy-side pieces moved to AG-07 and SF-06.\n\n## Old task IDs\n\nTasks keep their history when re-keyed, and old links redirect: MS-01→AG-01, MS-02→AG-02, MS-03→AG-03, IT-01→AG-04, IT-02→AG-05, IT-03→AG-06, IT-06→AG-08, MS-04→AG-09, MS-05→AG-10, MS-06→AG-11, CS-04→AG-12, IT-04→AG-13, SF-06→SF-08, SF-07→PM-09, PM-07↔PM-08 (swapped), NV-06→NV-08, NV-07→NV-06, SIM-04→SIM-06, SIM-05→SIM-04, SIM-06→SIM-05. Where an old key now names a different task (e.g. SF-06), the task page says so.","title":"Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"67dcca18-6dff-52a6-ac31-5494b4f0f8fb","document_id":"637321fe-e426-5b02-b948-cafe14395c3f","body":"# External Team Interfaces\n\nAutonomy depends on other teams for interfaces and data, never for us to build their systems. Each dependency is tracked on the 🧠 Autonomy General page with a status, a contact and our workaround.\n\n| Team | Provides to autonomy | Autonomy task | Workaround until delivered |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Controls | Motion command interface, enforced limits, status and faults (AG-07 contract) | AG-07, NV-02, AG-01 | Mock Controls node in simulation |\n| Controls | Excavation / deposition action servers | AG-02, AG-03 | Mock action servers |\n| Controls | Wheel odometry on hardware | SF-01 | Simulated drivetrain plugin |\n| Electrical | Sensor power and communication requirements; radar detection format | SF-05, SIM-04, PM-09 | Labeled assumptions |\n| Mechanical | Rover dimensions, mass properties, joints, mechanism constraints | SIM-02, PM-01, AG-03 | Clearly labeled approximations |\n| Hardware teams | Sensor specifications and mounting positions | SF-02, SIM-04 | Nominal CAD values, re-calibrated later |\n\n## Rules\n\n1. Autonomy never publishes motor-level commands (duty cycles, currents, actuator positions).\n2. Every motion request is timestamped; Controls rejects stale ones.\n3. Safe stop is a *request*; Controls executes it and re-enables motion.\n4. Interface documents live in `docs/interfaces/` and are versioned and reviewed by both teams.\n5. Autonomy completion metrics never count external work; external blockers are shown separately.","title":"External Team Interfaces","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"55af4e89-be25-5e91-96fd-dfca15a291b8","document_id":"6d2f1340-8af4-5216-88ad-557387252639","body":"# Team Onboarding\n\nWelcome to the Illinois Tech Lunabotics **Autonomy Team**. Start with [Autonomy Team Structure & Discord Channels](/docs/autonomy-team-structure).\n\n## Your first week\n1. Sign in to the Command Center and fill in your profile (skills, availability, GitHub username).\n2. Start the **Beginner to ROS 2 Contributor** learning path. You can claim a beginner task after module 5 — you don''t need to finish every path first.\n3. Read [Development Environment Setup](/docs/development-environment-setup) and [Git Workflow](/docs/git-workflow).\n4. Browse **Task Board → Available** and express interest in tasks that fit your track.\n\n## How work flows here\n- Every task is a guided assignment: read the *Why this matters*, study the referenced code, then work through the checklist.\n- Log progress after each work session — it helps reviewers and the next person.\n- A task is done only when a reviewer approves it against its Definition of Done. Merged PRs alone do not complete tasks.\n\n## Where to ask\nUse task discussions for technical questions so answers stay with the work.","title":"Team Onboarding","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"bc090583-6059-5ea5-96b5-604a69e04623","document_id":"02323238-403e-57d3-a170-cfe7053fcecc","body":"# Development Environment Setup\n\n> **Status:** draft. The ROS 2 distribution and Gazebo version are an open decision (see ADR \"Why ROS 2?\"). Update this page once decided.\n\n## Baseline (proposed)\n- Ubuntu LTS matching the chosen ROS 2 distribution\n- ROS 2 (Humble or Jazzy — decision pending)\n- Gazebo version paired with the ROS 2 distribution\n- colcon, rosdep, vcstool\n\n## Verify your install\n```bash\nros2 doctor\nros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker\n```\n\n## Workspace\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/lunabot_ws/src && cd ~/lunabot_ws\ncolcon build --symlink-install\nsource install/setup.bash\n```\n\nWindows/macOS members: document your working setup (VM, WSL2, container) here once verified.","title":"Development Environment Setup","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ce24f8fa-6339-5b2f-aed1-8a66c8f40389","document_id":"3e4e0897-1c37-52dc-bfff-3e0a927683b3","body":"# Git Workflow\n\n- Branch from `main`: `feature/<TASK-ID>-<short-slug>` — e.g. `feature/SF-01-sensor-fusion`.\n- Small, focused commits with imperative messages.\n- Open a PR titled `[TASK-ID] Summary` — e.g. `[SF-01] Implement initial localization estimator`.\n- Link the PR on the task page (GitHub section) so reviewers find it.\n- Rebase or merge `main` before requesting review; CI must pass.","title":"Git Workflow","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"427b87be-e97e-5bae-9808-c2ffabff9977","document_id":"340adb23-bc3a-5654-b4eb-77236869d707","body":"# Pull Request Standards\n\nEvery PR description includes:\n1. **Task** — link to the Command Center task.\n2. **What changed** — packages, nodes, parameters.\n3. **How to test** — exact commands.\n4. **Evidence** — plots, recordings, test output.\n5. **Interfaces** — any topic/message/frame changes (update the topic table).\n\nReviewers check functional correctness, documentation, tests, interface compatibility, performance, safety and integration readiness — the same dimensions used in task reviews.","title":"Pull Request Standards","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"559617d0-6c17-5409-b9b8-8a93710f3335","document_id":"2963146f-a287-5057-b1dc-6fd1ca9eba6c","body":"# ROS 2 Package Conventions (proposed — finalized by IT-01)\n\n- Package names: `lunabot_<area>` (snake_case).\n- Interfaces only in `lunabot_interfaces`.\n- Every tunable is a parameter; defaults live in `config/*.yaml`.\n- Pure logic in modules without ROS imports so it can be unit-tested.\n- Launch files in Python; accept `use_sim_time`.\n- Topics under subsystem namespaces: `/localization/*`, `/perception/*`, `/navigation/*`, `/mission/*`, `/autonomy/*` (requests to Controls). Controls-owned topics live under `/controls/*`.\n- QoS: SensorDataQoS for high-rate sensors; reliable + transient-local for state and health topics.","title":"ROS 2 Package Conventions","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"b0166621-ff34-5f43-8c27-e6dd2cec5227","document_id":"8802221a-846e-5ed8-bf0a-41e5d42e6c58","body":"# Coordinate Frame Conventions\n\nFollow REP-103 (units, axes) and REP-105 (mobile platform frames).\n\n```\nmap ──► odom ──► base_link ──► lidar_link\n                         ├──► imu_link\n                         ├──► camera_link ──► camera_optical_frame\n                         └──► (radar_link)\n```\n\n| Transform | Owner (proposed) |\n|---|---|\n| map → odom | Absolute localization (AprilTag/SLAM) or static identity in early sim |\n| odom → base_link | SF-01 EKF (drivetrain controller must NOT publish it) |\n| base_link → sensors | URDF (SIM-02) using calibration values (SF-02) |","title":"Coordinate Frame Conventions","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"b6e20e40-ab2c-5688-abaa-2bb5960bab70","document_id":"838a6a82-6d00-5e4e-8166-455d8d5f943a","body":"# Sensor Interfaces (illustrative)\n\n| Topic | Type | Frame | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| /lidar/points | sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2 | lidar_link | Per-point time needed for LIO de-skew |\n| /imu/data | sensor_msgs/msg/Imu | imu_link | Covariances must be filled |\n| /wheel/odometry | nav_msgs/msg/Odometry | odom → base_link | From Controls feedback on hardware (AG-07); from the drivetrain plugin in simulation |\n| /camera/image_raw | sensor_msgs/msg/Image | camera_optical_frame | |\n\nThese become verified once IT-01''s topic table is approved and matching code is merged.","title":"Sensor Interfaces","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"032ecc3b-f974-5b07-b227-520b29e95254","document_id":"3ddbfde6-2e32-5cde-9a41-3f90df3905e8","body":"# Localization Architecture\n\nWheel odometry + IMU (+ LIO, SF-03) → EKF/UKF (SF-01) → /odometry/filtered and odom → base_link.\nSF-04 monitors health and publishes OK/DEGRADED/LOST to mission logic and the arbiter.\n\nOpen question: absolute map anchoring (AprilTags vs SLAM vs known start pose) — see ADR \"Which localization algorithm?\".","title":"Localization Architecture","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"06786a36-9b6f-51b3-90b3-b9f1add04cf1","document_id":"2de121c5-abf6-5749-bbfd-4a7494201a38","body":"# Perception Architecture\n\nLiDAR → PM-02 preprocessing (filter, crop, voxel, accumulate) → PM-01 terrain grid (elevation, slope, roughness) → traversability OccupancyGrid → Nav2 costmaps.\nCameras → AprilTags (PM-03), optionally rock detection (PM-05).","title":"Perception Architecture","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"d348beae-fe56-583d-a97f-382894cb8d55","document_id":"405b4dea-750f-560e-8b59-5eb2ed672693","body":"# Navigation Architecture\n\nNav2 bt_navigator executes a behavior tree that plans (NV-01 planner) on the traversability costmap and follows with a local controller. Velocity output goes through the AG-07 adapter to /autonomy/cmd_vel; Controls (mock Controls in simulation) executes it. Recovery follows NV-06''s BT.","title":"Navigation Architecture","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"1dd48868-62cb-5803-aa83-4354e1f87e87","document_id":"cdcf3098-01b0-5da3-8804-c6cc5e38f44d","body":"# Simulation Setup\n\n```bash\nros2 launch lunabot_sim arena.launch.py scenario:=rocks seed:=42\n```\n(Illustrative — the package is delivered by SIM-01.)\n\nScenarios are seeded YAML files so results are reproducible. Use the lite world on laptops and in CI.","title":"Simulation Setup","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"54375f32-fafd-5ffb-b838-2448a474ca56","document_id":"72ba1078-d327-5cae-83e4-685f9f98cb86","body":"# Autonomy ↔ Controls Boundary\n\nAutonomy publishes **timestamped motion requests** on /autonomy/cmd_vel through the AG-07 adapter, sends **safe-stop requests**, and reads **ControlsStatus** (mode, motion enabled, E-stop active, enforced limits, faults).\n\nControls owns teleoperation, command arbitration, watchdogs, motor control, firmware and the physical emergency stop. Former tasks CS-01…CS-06 are archived for that reason.\n\n**Software stops never replace the hardware E-stop.** The hardware E-stop cuts actuator power independently of any computer and is Controls/Electrical-owned.\n\nSee [External Team Interfaces](/docs/external-team-interfaces) and AG-07.","title":"Autonomy ↔ Controls Boundary","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"741f43a9-3407-5868-8b43-9d82f5884c02","document_id":"6b18f653-a9bc-5255-b2ce-cda40f604ab9","body":"# Testing Standards\n\n- Pure logic has unit tests (`colcon test`).\n- Nodes have at least one launch/integration test or a documented replay test.\n- Benchmarks state machine, commit, scenario, seed and command.\n- Never report metrics without provenance; synthetic demo values must be labeled as such.","title":"Testing Standards","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"b2bf66c6-0493-5d0f-96d5-504938c82a40","document_id":"8c7d99db-fc69-54ac-8ee5-ad7720562be4","body":"# Competition Requirements and Verification\n\n**Rule of this page:** only requirements quoted from the *current* official NASA Lunabotics guidebook belong here, each with a section reference and the date it was checked. Other teams'' code is not a source of rules.\n\n| Requirement | Guidebook section | Verified on | Affects tasks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| _To be filled from the official guidebook_ | | | |\n\nInternal engineering targets (e.g. localization error goals) are **not** competition requirements and are tracked on tasks with rationale.","title":"Competition Requirements and Verification","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"9c1260f6-5aa9-5429-b390-ae1850e46129","document_id":"7757cfcd-0870-5a3a-b3d6-400209dfcd4d","body":"# Troubleshooting\n\n**No data on a topic** — check `ros2 topic info -v` for QoS mismatch.\n\n**TF flickering** — two publishers of the same transform (often odom → base_link). `ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames`.\n\n**Nodes ignore bag data** — missing `--clock` or `use_sim_time:=true`.\n\n**Robot explodes in Gazebo** — zero/tiny inertias in the URDF.","title":"Troubleshooting","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"56a26364-fd66-59e9-af7f-aac5ae6e7589","document_id":"042378b8-20dd-5e7f-b806-606479eb7823","body":"Decision record for the middleware choice.","title":"ADR: Why ROS 2?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"529bdefe-7a06-50e9-9832-03a4ac408457","document_id":"a468bd34-2552-52c8-aa09-9d0f078792b2","body":"Decision record for the baseline simulator.","title":"ADR: Why Gazebo as the baseline simulator?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"cafb7079-dbe3-5a0e-8c15-52767b60d563","document_id":"e584b2e0-2210-5233-a918-85c607f91c5c","body":"Decision record for localization.","title":"ADR: Which localization algorithm?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ea071c31-39cd-596b-be7b-4abc2c50e748","document_id":"f48890b4-5064-58c8-badb-0607b3dafab7","body":"Decision record for the global planner.","title":"ADR: Which navigation planner?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"7536782c-6993-594e-8bdb-ddc1e922073b","document_id":"b442a878-e2b6-5ce9-add0-ec778097295a","body":"Decision record for the sensor suite.","title":"ADR: Which sensors?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"c807ccf4-61a1-5854-bb7d-2e36bbd17ef8","document_id":"14f40b7f-363a-5710-a05c-34469b60a122","body":"Decision record for fallback behavior.","title":"ADR: What is the autonomy fallback policy?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"341c8b6a-10fa-5a9b-b3c8-3c0b5f9e2cc2","document_id":"14d3e1f0-4916-5dbf-8b77-38370f26ed0d","body":"Decision record for the end-to-end demonstration criteria.","title":"ADR: What constitutes a valid mission demonstration?","author_id":null,"summary":"Seeded starter content","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
insert into metric_definitions select * from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::metric_definitions, '[{"key":"ate_rmse","domain":"localization","name":"Absolute trajectory error (RMSE)","unit":"m","definition":"RMSE of position error after rigid alignment of estimated and ground-truth trajectories.","provenance":"evo_ape on TUM-format trajectories exported from a bag.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"851db193-1146-57ab-852a-3bcb0cf61681"},{"key":"rpe","domain":"localization","name":"Relative pose error","unit":"m","definition":"Error of relative motion over a fixed distance/time delta.","provenance":"evo_rpe with documented delta.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"2e582181-15a3-59cb-a1d7-190efa27e0f5"},{"key":"final_drift","domain":"localization","name":"Final drift","unit":"m","definition":"Distance between final estimated and true position.","provenance":"Last pose of estimate vs ground truth.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"4defcd9e-5ed3-53aa-8761-defe9c8e8576"},{"key":"loc_rate","domain":"localization","name":"Update frequency","unit":"Hz","definition":"Publish rate of the localization output.","provenance":"ros2 topic hz over 30 s.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"b51f888a-13f4-5ace-b3c6-742810b971cc"},{"key":"cpu_pct","domain":"localization","name":"CPU utilization","unit":"%","definition":"Mean CPU of the process during the run.","provenance":"psutil / top sampling at 1 Hz; machine documented.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"60c4030d-2f0c-5129-9db9-ee2cef2f71c3"},{"key":"plan_time","domain":"navigation","name":"Planning time","unit":"ms","definition":"Wall time to compute one global plan.","provenance":"Planner benchmark harness, median of runs.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"86a9e5b9-b296-5052-82df-39719eaefad7"},{"key":"path_length","domain":"navigation","name":"Path length","unit":"m","definition":"Sum of path segment lengths.","provenance":"Computed from nav_msgs/Path.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"43bd017b-9f75-55a3-b152-da24b35a599d"},{"key":"clearance","domain":"navigation","name":"Minimum clearance","unit":"m","definition":"Minimum distance from path to lethal cells.","provenance":"Distance transform of the costmap.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"f0173fb7-e54e-5546-b053-ca1c69072f77"},{"key":"collisions","domain":"navigation","name":"Collision count","unit":"count","definition":"Contacts between rover and obstacles.","provenance":"Simulator contact sensor.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"9b91ea36-dea6-54bd-92c4-e568e844c07e"},{"key":"goal_success","domain":"navigation","name":"Goal success rate","unit":"%","definition":"Goals reached within tolerance / goals sent.","provenance":"NavigateToPose results.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"b71c6e71-18d2-5843-8487-55bbf6af1aff"},{"key":"recovery_freq","domain":"navigation","name":"Recovery frequency","unit":"per run","definition":"Recovery behaviors executed per run.","provenance":"BT logs.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"031f1aff-ff43-5b10-835c-7a40470b2f2f"},{"key":"perc_latency","domain":"perception","name":"Processing latency","unit":"ms","definition":"Input header stamp to output publish.","provenance":"Stamp comparison in node.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"cf1afe22-4ea3-5297-a546-358510798a56"},{"key":"precision","domain":"perception","name":"Detection precision","unit":"%","definition":"TP / (TP + FP) — only where labeled data exists.","provenance":"Labeled evaluation set (source documented).","higher_is_better":true,"id":"5914b790-d379-52bb-9984-bcfa8a51c185"},{"key":"recall","domain":"perception","name":"Detection recall","unit":"%","definition":"TP / (TP + FN) — only where labeled data exists.","provenance":"Labeled evaluation set (source documented).","higher_is_better":true,"id":"61d39932-6cc8-50ac-98d4-149d43ceb25c"},{"key":"obstacle_coverage","domain":"perception","name":"Obstacle coverage","unit":"%","definition":"Known hazards marked lethal / known hazards.","provenance":"Simulation ground truth.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"df0e8bdc-4511-532d-88c9-843fd739d51b"},{"key":"false_lethal","domain":"perception","name":"False positives (lethal)","unit":"%","definition":"Known-free cells marked lethal / known-free cells.","provenance":"Simulation ground truth.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"4fa69d6c-aa01-5edb-92f0-a889b89c01cf"},{"key":"costmap_rate","domain":"perception","name":"Costmap update rate","unit":"Hz","definition":"Publish rate of the traversability grid.","provenance":"ros2 topic hz.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"ef19faae-a6b1-5479-a8d5-4061587dc571"},{"key":"tracking_error","domain":"control","name":"Trajectory tracking error","unit":"m","definition":"RMS lateral deviation from the reference path.","provenance":"Recorded pose vs path.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"4a202882-b030-50e7-932f-6879605a5d29"},{"key":"cmd_latency","domain":"control","name":"Command latency","unit":"ms","definition":"Sensor stamp to velocity command publish.","provenance":"Stamp propagation / tracing.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"5dd51f45-3175-5696-bf41-ad640a72dca3"},{"key":"stall_delay","domain":"control","name":"Stall detection delay","unit":"ms","definition":"Stall onset to fault published.","provenance":"Injected stall timestamp vs fault message.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"2de9c1c5-7939-5604-856d-244f91e70d60"},{"key":"estop_response","domain":"control","name":"Emergency-stop response","unit":"ms","definition":"E-stop message to zero /cmd_vel.","provenance":"Timestamps on both topics.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"80d15537-99cf-51d7-83a9-7bebba6f7002"},{"key":"rtf","domain":"simulation","name":"Real-time factor","unit":"ratio","definition":"Simulated time / wall time.","provenance":"Gazebo statistics.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"4497cb58-282a-5834-abda-8654740f56da"},{"key":"physics_rate","domain":"simulation","name":"Physics update rate","unit":"Hz","definition":"Physics steps per second.","provenance":"Simulator statistics.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"ff57a9e7-43cd-55b9-b6c8-f7f34b3d6bd5"},{"key":"sim_memory","domain":"simulation","name":"Memory consumption","unit":"MB","definition":"Resident memory of the simulator.","provenance":"Process sampling.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"5865fdbd-8b1c-5c46-936f-79858c66da9b"},{"key":"sensor_rate","domain":"simulation","name":"Sensor publication frequency","unit":"Hz","definition":"Rate of a simulated sensor topic.","provenance":"ros2 topic hz.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"8633e2b0-500e-5084-b73f-14274201b839"},{"key":"mission_completion","domain":"mission","name":"Mission completion rate","unit":"%","definition":"Missions meeting pre-defined pass criteria / missions run.","provenance":"IT-06 suite results.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"cd1ec2b2-e363-56d5-a9fa-cb168584dff3"},{"key":"cycles","domain":"mission","name":"Successful cycles","unit":"count","definition":"Completed excavate→deposit cycles.","provenance":"Mission state log.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"8ba47981-16c9-53a7-95fe-1c9abd8065d7"},{"key":"mission_runtime","domain":"mission","name":"Mission runtime","unit":"min","definition":"Start to DONE/SAFE_STOP.","provenance":"Mission state timestamps.","higher_is_better":false,"id":"cd02ecea-e97c-5316-8235-39809d8be091"},{"key":"recovery_count","domain":"mission","name":"Recovery count","unit":"count","definition":"Successful recoveries per mission.","provenance":"Mission/BT logs.","higher_is_better":true,"id":"6d11acff-f672-5fc7-bd25-320613266a9f"}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
insert into integration_components select * from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::integration_components, '[{"key":"drv-lidar","group":"sensors","name":"LiDAR driver","purpose":"Publishes 3D point clouds from the LiDAR (or Gazebo sensor).","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/lidar/points","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["frame_id","rate"],"task_keys":["SIM-01","SIM-05"],"id":"8b6531ab-0d4f-56e1-8bbe-ed4da3bdb17c","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"drv-camera","group":"sensors","name":"Camera driver","purpose":"Publishes images and calibration.","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/camera/image_raw","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Image","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/camera/camera_info","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/CameraInfo","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["frame_id","resolution"],"task_keys":["PM-03"],"id":"2eda9fd4-66c9-5ad8-8c01-214649a2e3a6","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"drv-imu","group":"sensors","name":"IMU driver","purpose":"Publishes angular velocity, linear acceleration and (optionally) orientation with covariance.","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/imu/data","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Imu","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["frame_id","rate"],"task_keys":["SF-01"],"id":"044a39e9-e807-57a9-9574-c8e7fc56dcac","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"drv-encoders","group":"sensors","name":"Wheel encoders / wheel odometry","purpose":"Controls-owned on hardware: wheel odometry delivered through the AG-07 feedback interface. In simulation the drivetrain plugin publishes it.","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/wheel/odometry","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["published by Controls"],"task_keys":["AG-07","SIM-02"],"id":"d9812cb4-6925-53be-a61e-372594b705a1","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"drv-radar","group":"sensors","name":"Radar (optional)","purpose":"Sparse detections for dust robustness — pending SF-05 feasibility. Driver integration is Electrical''s.","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/radar/detections","type":"TBD","note":"pending SF-05"}],"parameters":[],"task_keys":["SF-05","PM-09"],"id":"f8374cad-f8c5-5a51-b98d-4144b9acd17f","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"loc-confidence","group":"localization","name":"Localization confidence view","purpose":"Publishes covariance ellipses, freshness and drift (sim) for debugging and AG-06.","inputs":[{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"},{"name":"/localization/health","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticStatus","note":"proposed; may become a custom msg"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/localization/covariance_marker","type":"visualization_msgs/msg/Marker"}],"parameters":["ellipse_sigma"],"task_keys":["SF-07"],"id":"5e11ac0d-d717-529f-a085-8677ab145136","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"loc-fusion","group":"localization","name":"Sensor fusion (EKF/UKF)","purpose":"Fuses wheel odometry, IMU and LIO into a continuous pose with covariance; owns odom → base_link.","inputs":[{"name":"/wheel/odometry","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/imu/data","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Imu","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/lio/odometry","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"},{"name":"/tf odom→base_link","type":"tf2_msgs/msg/TFMessage"}],"parameters":["frequency","two_d_mode","odom0_config","imu0_config"],"task_keys":["SF-01","SF-03","SF-08","SF-06"],"id":"0cfc22b1-d162-5524-9a9d-223a24b2a727","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"loc-tf","group":"localization","name":"TF tree","purpose":"Static sensor transforms (calibration/URDF) and dynamic odom/map transforms.","inputs":[{"name":"/joint_states","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/JointState"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/tf","type":"tf2_msgs/msg/TFMessage"},{"name":"/tf_static","type":"tf2_msgs/msg/TFMessage"}],"parameters":["robot_description"],"task_keys":["SF-02","SIM-02","AG-04"],"id":"7a761cd6-c073-5754-987f-609e4eb5b116","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"loc-health","group":"localization","name":"Localization health","purpose":"Monitors input age and covariance; publishes OK/DEGRADED/LOST.","inputs":[{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"},{"name":"/imu/data","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Imu","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/wheel/odometry","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"proposed"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/localization/health","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticStatus","note":"proposed; may become a custom msg"}],"parameters":["input_timeouts_s","cov_warn","cov_critical","recovery_hold_s"],"task_keys":["SF-04"],"id":"9b093f06-d0c6-5352-bf56-d6f2e74448b5","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"per-cloud","group":"perception","name":"Point cloud processing","purpose":"Filters, crops, downsamples and optionally accumulates clouds.","inputs":[{"name":"/lidar/points","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/tf","type":"tf2_msgs/msg/TFMessage"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/perception/points_filtered","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2"}],"parameters":["voxel_leaf_m","crop_box","accumulate_frames"],"task_keys":["PM-02"],"id":"61578aca-95a1-5796-9baf-85d1b9f4409e","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"per-terrain","group":"perception","name":"Terrain mapping","purpose":"Elevation, slope and roughness layers.","inputs":[{"name":"/perception/points_filtered","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/perception/elevation","type":"nav_msgs/msg/OccupancyGrid"}],"parameters":["resolution_m","window_m"],"task_keys":["PM-01","PM-06"],"id":"7b7d5228-05c3-597c-86db-8539b3e98ac5","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"per-obstacles","group":"perception","name":"Obstacle detection","purpose":"Rock/obstacle detection and multi-sensor association.","inputs":[{"name":"/camera/image_raw","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Image","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/perception/points_filtered","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/perception/obstacles","type":"TBD (proposed)"}],"parameters":[],"task_keys":["PM-05","PM-08","PM-09"],"id":"027c96b3-7c0b-5124-a812-be5c634f7fc8","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"per-costmap","group":"perception","name":"Traversability costmap","purpose":"Nav2-compatible cost grid: free / lethal / unknown with inflation.","inputs":[{"name":"/perception/elevation","type":"nav_msgs/msg/OccupancyGrid"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/perception/traversability","type":"nav_msgs/msg/OccupancyGrid","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["lethal_slope_deg","roughness_lethal_m","inflation_radius_m"],"task_keys":["PM-01"],"id":"619b82aa-57b0-5373-b769-d5cc7b205059","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"per-tags","group":"perception","name":"AprilTag localization","purpose":"Absolute pose fixes from fiducials (subject to rules).","inputs":[{"name":"/camera/image_raw","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/Image","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/camera/camera_info","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/CameraInfo","note":"proposed"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/localization/tag_pose","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/PoseWithCovarianceStamped"}],"parameters":["tag_family","tag_size_m"],"task_keys":["PM-03"],"id":"72b6d9ef-6841-5a26-b50f-6271b5758332","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"nav-global","group":"navigation","name":"Global planner","purpose":"Computes paths over the costmap (A* / S-Theta*).","inputs":[{"name":"/perception/traversability","type":"nav_msgs/msg/OccupancyGrid","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/mission/goal_pose","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped","note":"proposed"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/plan","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Path"}],"parameters":["turn_penalty","terrain_weight"],"task_keys":["NV-01","NV-04"],"id":"f2562492-c3d7-502d-8d09-6d2980342718","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"nav-local","group":"navigation","name":"Local controller","purpose":"Tracks the path producing velocity commands.","inputs":[{"name":"/plan","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Path"},{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/autonomy/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/TwistStamped","note":"autonomy motion request — AG-07 contract (proposed)"}],"parameters":["controller plugin","lookahead"],"task_keys":["NV-02","NV-05"],"id":"6dda6d0b-67d2-5f35-b2b4-7215d3dc5611","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"nav-recovery","group":"navigation","name":"Recovery manager (BT)","purpose":"Replanning and recovery behaviors in the Nav2 behavior tree.","inputs":[{"name":"/plan","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Path"}],"outputs":[{"name":"navigate_to_pose","type":"nav2_msgs/action/NavigateToPose"}],"parameters":["number_of_retries"],"task_keys":["NV-02","NV-06","NV-08"],"id":"beddd547-a504-5a7b-984c-6285cb8e691b","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"mis-fsm","group":"mission","name":"Mission state machine","purpose":"Decides the next required action: localize, select goal, navigate, request excavation/deposition, confirm, recover, safe stop. Never commands motors.","inputs":[{"name":"/localization/health","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticStatus","note":"proposed; may become a custom msg"},{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/mission/state","type":"std_msgs/msg/String","note":"proposed; custom msg in AG-04"},{"name":"/mission/goal_pose","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/autonomy/safe_stop_request","type":"std_msgs/msg/Bool","note":"autonomy asks Controls to stop — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"parameters":["max_cycles","state_timeouts_s"],"task_keys":["AG-01","AG-10"],"id":"5ca6efc5-10bd-5cde-9fc7-6902bc847687","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"mis-goals","group":"mission","name":"Goal & zone selection","purpose":"Chooses excavation/deposition targets inside verified zones.","inputs":[{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"},{"name":"/perception/traversability","type":"nav_msgs/msg/OccupancyGrid","note":"proposed"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/mission/goal_pose","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped","note":"proposed"}],"parameters":["arena_layout","weights"],"task_keys":["NV-03","AG-09"],"id":"e95483ae-a3c5-5b12-aa67-5c9b18bc7ec3","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"mis-excavate","group":"mission","name":"Excavation action client","purpose":"Autonomy side of the excavation contract: checks preconditions, requests, monitors, handles outcomes. The server (dig sequence) is Controls''.","inputs":[{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"excavate","type":"lunabot_interfaces/action/Excavate (client)"}],"parameters":["client_timeout_s"],"task_keys":["AG-02","AG-11"],"id":"069ed5fd-c9b0-579b-9a58-82599a8ac291","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"mis-deposit","group":"mission","name":"Deposition coordinator","purpose":"Positions and validates alignment, then requests the deposit. The dump sequence (server) is Controls''.","inputs":[{"name":"/odometry/filtered","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"robot_localization default"},{"name":"/localization/health","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticStatus","note":"proposed; may become a custom msg"}],"outputs":[{"name":"deposit","type":"lunabot_interfaces/action/Deposit (client)"}],"parameters":["align_tolerance_deg"],"task_keys":["AG-03"],"id":"6dc51400-f2e1-5650-b8cb-75ad9e82ed23","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"ctl-interface","group":"control","name":"Autonomy ↔ Controls interface","purpose":"Autonomy-owned adapter: stamps and clamps motion requests to the limits Controls advertises, forwards safe-stop requests, surfaces Controls status. Mock Controls stands in during simulation.","inputs":[{"name":"/navigation/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist"},{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/autonomy/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/TwistStamped","note":"autonomy motion request — AG-07 contract (proposed)"},{"name":"/autonomy/safe_stop_request","type":"std_msgs/msg/Bool","note":"autonomy asks Controls to stop — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"parameters":["command_validity_s","publish_rate_hz"],"task_keys":["AG-07","AG-12"],"id":"ccf35530-ae7e-564e-80ba-7ade720f1cb7","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"},{"key":"ctl-arbiter","group":"control","name":"Command arbitration (Controls)","purpose":"Controls-owned: chooses between teleop and autonomy requests, enforces timeouts and the E-stop. Shown for interface context only.","inputs":[{"name":"/autonomy/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/TwistStamped","note":"autonomy motion request — AG-07 contract (proposed)"},{"name":"/cmd_vel/teleop","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist","note":"Controls-owned (external)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist","note":"Controls-owned input (external)"}],"parameters":["owned by Controls"],"task_keys":["AG-07"],"id":"5330e501-f66a-533a-b8f2-db7e9f67b122","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"ctl-drive","group":"control","name":"Drivetrain control (Controls)","purpose":"Controls-owned: velocity → wheel commands, PID, limits, wheel odometry. Autonomy only consumes its feedback.","inputs":[{"name":"/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist","note":"Controls-owned input (external)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/wheel/odometry","type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry","note":"proposed"},{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"parameters":["owned by Controls"],"task_keys":["AG-07"],"id":"cabff3e3-9a98-5f9c-afbd-cc56898012f9","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"ctl-hw","group":"control","name":"Motor drivers & firmware (Controls/Electrical)","purpose":"Hardware interface, motor drivers and firmware. In simulation the SIM-02 drivetrain plugin replaces it.","inputs":[{"name":"command interfaces","type":"Controls-internal"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/joint_states","type":"sensor_msgs/msg/JointState"}],"parameters":["owned by Controls/Electrical"],"task_keys":["SIM-02"],"id":"db51f193-2f20-5d51-8fa3-7f5e759c774e","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"saf-watchdog","group":"safety","name":"Command watchdogs (Controls)","purpose":"Controls-owned: stop motion when autonomy requests go stale. Autonomy''s side is the validity window in AG-07.","inputs":[{"name":"/autonomy/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/TwistStamped","note":"autonomy motion request — AG-07 contract (proposed)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/cmd_vel","type":"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist","note":"Controls-owned input (external)"}],"parameters":["owned by Controls"],"task_keys":["AG-07"],"id":"c93ea195-0012-5c46-b56d-dc941f60a043","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"saf-estop","group":"safety","name":"Emergency stop (Controls/Electrical)","purpose":"Physical E-stop hardware and its software state are Controls/Electrical-owned. Autonomy reads estop_active from ControlsStatus and enters SAFE_STOP.","inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"parameters":["owned by Controls/Electrical"],"task_keys":["AG-07"],"id":"0ace2c90-acd6-5fa7-b420-604f8946a998","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Controls"},{"key":"saf-faults","group":"safety","name":"Autonomy fault monitoring","purpose":"Aggregates localization health, navigation failures and Controls-reported faults into decisions for mission logic and the operator view.","inputs":[{"name":"/localization/health","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticStatus","note":"proposed; may become a custom msg"},{"name":"/controls/status","type":"lunabot_interfaces/msg/ControlsStatus","note":"motion enabled, limits, faults — AG-07 (proposed)"}],"outputs":[{"name":"/diagnostics","type":"diagnostic_msgs/msg/DiagnosticArray"}],"parameters":[],"task_keys":["SF-04","AG-10","NV-06"],"id":"5706bc7a-e866-5e77-b5f4-e91dd1159347","owner_id":null,"interface_status":"illustrative","owner_team":"Autonomy"}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
insert into external_dependencies select * from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::external_dependencies, '[{"team":"Controls","title":"Motion command interface, status and faults","description":"Controls'' side of the AG-07 contract: accept timestamped velocity requests, enforce limits, publish ControlsStatus and honor safe-stop requests.","needs":["Accept geometry_msgs/TwistStamped on /autonomy/cmd_vel and reject requests older than the agreed validity window","Publish ControlsStatus (mode, motion_enabled, estop_active, max velocities, faults) at ≥ 10 Hz","Implement the safe-stop request service and report the result","Agree fault codes"],"workaround":"mock_controls.py in simulation (AG-07).","id":"38792e10-c4b4-5cd1-a864-5fafc0b06503","task_ids":["e5839c37-c400-51c0-b926-2e44b2993145","3f3aa0af-f122-53ba-b2d5-514fa557a5d3","20c6ab88-05ca-5add-b926-411b30386c9c"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"team":"Controls","title":"Excavation and deposition action servers","description":"Real implementations of Excavate.action and Deposit.action as documented in docs/interfaces/.","needs":["Implement the agreed action definitions","Report reason codes for failures (stall, timeout, fault)","Report a material estimate when available","Honor cancellation within an agreed time"],"workaround":"Mock action servers with configurable outcomes (AG-02, AG-03).","id":"61866fc5-ab84-5269-9fea-7de94b132cd5","task_ids":["c4795d19-bd20-5bdd-9bfd-253e4fc310ab","7bafdba8-75f3-5a8d-ac0a-9882a055c76e"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"team":"Controls","title":"Wheel odometry feedback on hardware","description":"nav_msgs/Odometry from wheel encoders with covariance, published by Controls on the real rover.","needs":["Publish /wheel/odometry with filled twist covariance","Do not publish the odom → base_link transform (SF-01 owns it)","Document encoder resolution and wheel geometry used"],"workaround":"Simulated drivetrain plugin (SIM-02).","id":"27fefdc1-4960-53d2-9407-c03d6d137c69","task_ids":["ad5ad035-2683-5642-9a09-3ec5b942a38e"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"team":"Mechanical","title":"Rover dimensions, mass properties and mechanism constraints","description":"Authoritative geometry for the simulation model, costmap footprint and deposition alignment.","needs":["Overall dimensions and footprint","Mass and inertia estimates","Wheel radius, track width, wheelbase","Joint axes and limits of the excavation/deposition mechanism","Sensor mounting positions","Deposition approach direction and alignment tolerance"],"workaround":"Clearly labeled approximations in SIM-02 (config/approximations.yaml).","id":"f0ad5952-aa39-5389-b48c-cb2b1bc6c496","task_ids":["c37c65ff-e04e-5bfa-954c-54142f9de733","9a90482b-015a-5d7a-89b9-149227bf65a7","7bafdba8-75f3-5a8d-ac0a-9882a055c76e"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"team":"Electrical","title":"Sensor power and communication requirements","description":"How sensors connect and are synchronized, so simulation and drivers match reality.","needs":["Interface per sensor (Ethernet/USB/serial) and data rates","Time synchronization approach","Radar detection output format if radar is adopted"],"workaround":"Documented assumptions in SIM-04 and SF-05.","id":"a503d24a-09de-5b97-ab35-3541a1bfbd9b","task_ids":["3edf045c-1999-5599-9447-b50de03cf966","200c6aa3-aa3a-5c0f-a86c-3a4996adc549","83662f45-9f4c-58a7-a326-95399a8568ba"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"},{"team":"Hardware","title":"Sensor specifications and mounting","description":"Exact sensor models and mounting poses for calibration and simulation fidelity.","needs":["LiDAR, camera and IMU models with datasheets","Mounting positions and orientations (from CAD)","Field of view and update rates"],"workaround":"Nominal CAD values; recalibrate with SF-02 once hardware exists.","id":"a5add4a8-ce7b-5f9b-aa39-f6eb93211e5a","task_ids":["f05ffa4c-b505-5dda-a737-b97c3901fca2","200c6aa3-aa3a-5c0f-a86c-3a4996adc549"],"status":"not_requested","contact":"","notes":"","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T12:00:00.000Z"}]'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
